+
+## Context / Decisions
+
+First brick of iPhone Duo support (#26). Lays the posture plumbing and the keypad edges. Other postures (#67, #68, #69) plug into it.
+
+Mockups: closed https://claude.ai/artifact/JxLVV5v8VvnnmoUfHtKxof · flat https://claude.ai/artifact/NLrVCWx2Fd6jHdemQnwy9U
+
+- Native APIs only. No hard-coded device sizes, no special cases per device.
+- Keypad edges: vertical `.regular` → keypad ignores the horizontal safe area on both sides, 14 pt from the physical edge (touch rules only, Mac never). Vertical compact → each side ignores it unless an `.occlusion` region (`reservedRegions`) crosses the keypad's height on that side (round 2, prototype approved: https://claude.ai/artifact/Qo5eGsX1fS8LvgDPXtLPrh).
+  - vR: any iPhone portrait (no side safe area, Dynamic Island above the keypad: no change), Duo closed portrait, Duo open, iPad (no change).
+  - C/C (iPhone landscape, Duo closed landscape): per side, by occlusion (round 2). Side crossed by the camera or Dynamic Island keeps the safe area, other side 14 pt.
+  - Synchronous: right on the first frame, no launch jump.
+- Occlusion read in vertical compact only, never the hinge. Generic: no device check. vR ignores occlusions (closed portrait graze stays out). Accepted: landscape launch jump (regions arrive 76–180 ms after the first frame, no earlier API), iPhone landscape asymmetric (Dynamic Island side keeps its margin).
+- Hinge (`onHingeChange`) and `.division` only decide posture modes in `HingeRule` (no hinge or closed → `SizeClassRule`, fully open landscape → `.wide`). Never the edges.
+- Expanded: status line follows the keypad edges (lines up with it), and the gap status line ↔ keypad equals Compact's (status line rests on the keypad, no longer centered on the X line). Applies to iPhone landscape and iPad too.
+- Stack keeps the safe area.
+- Clean, small, composable: one job per type, one file each.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- Duo closed portrait: no layout jump at launch; keypad 14 pt from both edges, function pager full width, page 2 never visible.
+- Duo closed landscape, camera top-left: keypad 14 pt from the left edge (under the camera), right side unchanged. Camera bottom-right: identical to before (left already 14 pt, right keeps the safe area since the camera crosses the `+` row).
+- Duo open flat landscape: Expanded keypad 14 pt from both edges, status line aligned with it.
+- Expanded (Duo open, iPhone landscape, iPad): gap between status line and keypad equals Compact's.
+- Rotating or folding live switches layout; shift, current page and entry survive.
+- iPhone 18 Pro portrait: identical to before. Landscape: side without Dynamic Island 14 pt from the edge, Dynamic Island side keeps the safe area; flips with rotation.
+- Tests: posture modes; edges on in vR; in C/C, per-side edges from occlusion frames vs keypad band (none crossing → both, crossing on one side → the other only).
+
+## Implementation
+
+- `Core/Layout/Hinge/HingeStatus.swift`, `Core/Layout/Rules/HingeRule.swift`: no hinge or closed → `SizeClassRule`, fully open landscape → `.wide`. `#Playground` per posture.
+- `LayoutContext` + `hingeStatus`, `divisionAxis`, `containerAxis` (open Duo is R/R both ways).
+- `LayoutModeRule.keypadEdgeReach(in:)` (round 2, replaced round 1's `keypadReachesScreenEdges`): `HingeRule` delegates to `SizeClassRule`; `ChosenModeRule` → `.safeArea`. Travels as `\.keypadEdgeReach`.
+- `UI/ViewModifiers/Layout/Hinge/`: `HingeStatusChangeModifier`, `DivisionAxisChangeModifier`, behind `if #available(anyAppleOS 27.1, *)`. `KeypadLayoutModifier` stays the only environment reader.
+- `UI/ViewModifiers/Layout/Edges/KeypadScreenEdgesModifier.swift`: `ignoresSafeArea(.container, edges:)` with the edges `KeypadEdgeReach` computes (round 2).
+- `CalculatorView` Expanded: status line `.padding(.leading, margin).keypadScreenEdges(alongside: keypadSpan)`, no xLineHeight frame; stack `.padding(.trailing, margin)`.
+- `CalculatorCoordinator`: iOS injects `HingeRule()`.
+- Removed in round 1: occlusion clearance (`OcclusionClearanceChangeModifier`, `EdgeInsetsExtension`, `CGRectExtension` + tests).
+- Tests: `HingeRuleTests`, `AxisExtensionTests`, `SizeClassRuleTests`, `ChosenModeRuleTests`.
+- Build ✅ · tests ✅ (635) · SwiftLint ✅ · archtest ✅.
+- Round 2 (occlusion edges): `Core/Layout/Edges/KeypadEdgeReach.swift` (`.safeArea` / `.screenEdges` / `.unoccludedScreenEdges`, pure `ignoredEdges(clearOf:alongside:)`), `Core/Layout/Edges/Occlusions/ScreenOcclusion.swift` (side + vertical span, `crosses(_:)`), `UI/ViewModifiers/Layout/Edges/Occlusions/ScreenOcclusionsModifier.swift` (full-screen `reservedRegions(kind: .occlusion)` reader → `\.screenOcclusions`, behind `#available(anyAppleOS 27.1, *)`). `LayoutModeRule.keypadReachesScreenEdges` → `keypadEdgeReach(in:)` (SizeClassRule: regular → `.screenEdges`, compact → `.unoccludedScreenEdges`; HingeRule delegates; ChosenModeRule → `.safeArea`). `KeypadScreenEdgesModifier` takes `alongside keypadSpan`; `CalculatorView` measures the keypad span once, keypad and status line share it. `CalculatorCoordinator` adds `.screenOcclusions()`. Tests: `KeypadEdgeReachTests` (7), `ScreenOcclusionTests` (4), rule tests updated.
+- Round 2: build ✅ · tests ✅ (647) · SwiftLint ✅ · archtest ✅.
+
+## Review
+
+### Round validation · 2026-11-09
+
+Scope: `origin/develop...HEAD`, 24 code files + task file. LENSES: style ✓ · elegance ✓ · structure ✓ · correctness ✓.
+
+- 🟠 [correctness] `ScreenOcclusionsModifier.swift`: below 27.1 occlusions stayed `[]` ("none"), so vertical compact ignored both sides (keypad under Dynamic Island / camera on 27.0). Autofix: occlusions `[ScreenOcclusion]?`, `nil` until read → safe area kept; test added. Fixed.
+- 🟡 [style] task file: C/C decision bullet stale (pre round 2). Fixed.
